<title>UK: SBC Warburg clarifies view on Wolseley.</title>
<headline>SBC Warburg clarifies view on Wolseley.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>SBC Warburg on Wednesday clarified its investment view on Wolseley Plc, denying market suggestions that it viewed the international building supplies group as a &quot;sell&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;SBC Warburg is a buyer not a seller of Wolseley,&quot; said analyst Mark Stockdale at the investment bank. Earlier Warburg had declined to comment on the rumours.</p>
<p>The stock slipped 3p to 468p, after Merrill Lynch cut its profit forecast for Wolseley.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
